==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|ku}}

===Etymology===
*From the stem ''ku-'' and the particle ''[[-kaan]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*Hyphenation: ku•kaan

===Indefinite pronoun===
'''kukaan'''
#(''In question clauses'') [[anybody]], [[anyone]]:
#:*Tietääkö '''kukaan''', missä se on?
#:**Does ''anybody'' know where it is?
#(''With the negative verb ([[en]], [[et]], [[ei]], [[emme]], [[ette]], [[eivät]])'') [[no-one]], [[none]], [[nobody]]:
#:*'''Kukaan''' ''[[ei]]'' [[haluta|halua]] [[sellainen|sellaista]] [[tulevaisuus|tulevaisuutta]] [[lapsi]]lleen.
#:**''None'' wants that kind of future for their children.

====Inflection====
*All the cases of ''kukaan'', except for the nominative singular, are old-fashioned. They can sometimes be used just to arouse listeners' or readers' attention. In modern Finnish those cases have been replaced by the corresponding cases of ''kenkään'' &ndash; the nominative ''kenkään'' is, however, used only in poetic language, and even there very infrequently.
*Several of the singular cases of "ken" can be shortened by dropping -'''en''' from the stem, e.g. ''kenellekään'' > ''kellekään''. 
*Note that unlike most Finnish nominals, "kenkään" has a specific [[accusative]] form, '''''kenetkään'''''.
*There are also the abessive cases, but they are very infrequently used.

